location would be hidden without outside spells being required. A side benifit is that by default all familiars would be materialized as twilight doesn't exist by default.<br /> <br /> It may be a truth hidden from the students with their arrival covering up the truth.<br /> <br /> The downside is that'd mean that the whole school could be dispelled so I'm not sold on if this would be the best choice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yikes, dispelling the school is a terrifying thought. I wonder if Space can be used to prevent it from being located by map. Probably Space, practice of Unmaking to obliterate the location. Veiling is probably safer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T21:02:14-07:00","id":901707,"title":"","content":"Ya the best solution to that so far is cast at potency 5. Not exactly a perfect solution but possible for a Gnosis 5 space 5 casting at 6x ritual length and out of a grimoire with yantras.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2909,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","user":"Mr.F.I.X.","date":". 05-28-2016, 12:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T21:55:55-07:00","id":901737,"title":"","content":"Hogwarts is under a Veiling effect, or possibly Co-Location, at one point someone mentions that a Muggle travelling to the school would find a ruined castle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T22:21:21-07:00","id":901753,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a> I know that technically speaking Hogwarts itself is under a veiling spell but considering that other aspects of the wizarding world seem to exists in folded spaces I thought I'd present it as an idea. I admit diagonally would be more suited to be represented as a pocket dimension than hogwarts itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T14:29:17-07:00","id":902287,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I'd be tempted to just call Hogwarts and other such locations as being a form of verge in this universe, inherently magical locations that mages may have added effects to, but not necessarily created themselves. These hidden/obscured/extra-dimensional/ect. spaces would then serve as inherent mysteries for generation after generation of mages and reasons why they have become inhabited hotspots of the wizarding world. Unlike CoD verges, CoWW (Chronicles of Wizarding World) verges wouldn't need to be tied to a specific Path, but could be.<br /> <br /> If you say Hogwarts is inherently veiled, then perhaps studing this mystery is where much of veiling magic comes from, same if you say Hogwarts is hidden in a pocket realm, studying it has lead to mages being able to enchant tents with bigger insides and houses hidden between addresses.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3385-ckobbe","name":"ckobbe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T17:05:01-07:00","id":1107151,"title":"","content":"At some point I began imagining a Hogwarts like school of magic based on the 5 Watchtowers. I didn't refine the traits and aesthetics of these Watchtower based houses though, they were mainly just passing thoughts and ideas. The one I mainly thought about was Stygia/Moros/The Tower of the Lead Coin.<br /> <br /> For example, Moros of the House of The Lead Coin would be associated with determination, hard work, pragmatism, ingenuity, invention and science. Members of this house are usually very open-minded and accepting of new ideas and the concepts of death and the afterlife. The aesthetics would have involved lots of carved stone, wood and marble, dour looking gardens and crypt-like surroundings with symbols of the afterlife and skeletal themed statuettes, finely crafted, sturdy wood and marble bookcases and fine decoration and furnitures, with a large number of portraits, statues and busts of deceased great people, with ample ghosts present. Experimentation with machinery and alchemy and communication with the dead are common to this House. House Robes and general color schemes, for heraldry and decoration, are grey, purple and black.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9207-lord-proteus","user":"Lord Proteus","date":". 06-23-2017, 08:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9207-lord-proteus","name":"Lord Proteus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T18:11:22-07:00","id":1107165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Proteus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/887185-hogwarts-the-wizarding-world-chronicle-2e?p=1107151#post1107151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At some point I began imagining a Hogwarts like school of magic based on the 5 Watchtowers. I didn't refine the traits and aesthetics of these Watchtower based houses though, they were mainly just passing thoughts and ideas. The one I mainly thought about was Stygia/Moros/The Tower of the Lead Coin.<br /> <br /> For example, Moros of the House of The Lead Coin would be associated with determination, hard work, pragmatism, ingenuity, invention and science. Members of this house are usually very open-minded and accepting of new ideas and the concepts of death and the afterlife.....House Robes and general color schemes, for heraldry and decoration, are grey, purple and black.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or Blue. The traits you are describing are considered typical of a Ravenclaw in the Potterverse. Slytherin maps pretty well to Mastigos and Gryffindor maps to Obrimos. Hufflepuff are...illl defined.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T18:15:49-07:00","id":1107166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/887185-hogwarts-the-wizarding-world-chronicle-2e?p=1107165#post1107165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or Blue. The traits you are describing are considered typical of a Ravenclaw in the Potterverse. Slytherin maps pretty well to Mastigos and Gryffindor maps to Obrimos. Hufflepuff are...illl defined.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually I think Hard work and determination are Hufflepuff traits. If Ravenclaw is the house of Scientists and Scholars, Hufflepuff is the house of Builders and Tradesmen.<br /> <br /> My ideas were not meant to be regarded as simply skin-swapping the Hogwarts houses with the Towers and Paths. That Ravenclaw and my depiction of Moros share a lot of common ground is just coincidence.<br /> <br /> For Mastigos for visuals I was thinking cathedral-like architecture and lots of gargoyles and twisted, abstract and thought provoking art, with Red and maybe White as their primary colors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9207-lord-proteus","user":"Lord Proteus","date":". 06-23-2017, 09:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9207-lord-proteus","name":"Lord Proteus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-23T18:34:23-07:00","id":1107168,"title":"","content":"Fair emougj: just wanted to offer some assistance. Would have thought Obrimos would have claimed the warmer colours though; reds, yellows and bright colours that 'pop'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:",