userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T10:05:31-07:00","id":1107674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/887185-hogwarts-the-wizarding-world-chronicle-2e?p=1107656#post1107656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, this is neat. One thing my setting hack is missing is pure blood wizarding families as proximii. I'll have to sub to your thread!</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. It is more based around the general concept of &quot;magic school&quot; than any specific example, and around Proximi as opposed to full Mages (as Mage numbers in the area are limited due to... reasons). I'm just trying to come up with the Proximus Houses/Dynasties that provide membership to the school right now.<br /> <br /> I've got some ideas on the Obrimos one (The Trevelyan family) - focusing on Prime's relationship to Truth, they are the &quot;honest to a fault&quot; students/alumni... except when they aren't. Their curse manifests in a compulsion to keep their word and tell no lies. Violate that (or trigger Paradox), and a split personality takes over - with inverted Virtue and Vice - that they have distorted recollections of. So, very trustworthy, unless their evil side/twin takes over.<br /> <br /> Moros might be Archivists, Engineers, or Finance. Goth themes optional. Thyrsus are going to fill the Athletic and Personable niche. Not sure on the Mastigos and Acanthus ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T12:35:30-07:00","id":1107712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/887185-hogwarts-the-wizarding-world-chronicle-2e?p=1107672#post1107672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#1D2129\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"http://www.harrypotter.bloomsbury.com/uk/harrypotter20/\" target=\"_blank\">Tomorrow is 20th anniversary for the premier of first Harry Potter books</a> - How do you plan to celebrate it? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>By becoming a Dark Wizard and killing Harry Potter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9207-lord-proteus","name":"Lord Proteus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T09:00:36-07:00","id":1108417,"title":"","content":"One quibble: The first part of Muggle Empathy makes zero sense if the wizard is from a wizarding family or otherwise was raises in the culture. Kind of puts a mechanical constraint on building a backstory for wizard for the house or accepting a loss of beat generation for yourself. The other Houses have more action or personality driven ones. Someone can come from a long line of wizards or be a muggle born who learned magic was real the month before you showed up and still be strongly driven to be a social leader or want to fight or love mysteries and want to learn more about the world around you.<br /> <br /> But of those two hypothetical students, only the muggle born one would be able to benefit from the ignorance part of Muggle Empathy. Also it would necessarily become less and less of a thing over the years of school, so it would be reduced in value IC for anyone.<br /> <br /> I'm enjoying the thought you've put into this though and might try and put it on my to do GM list sometime in the future. Thanks!<br /> <br /> <u>Edited for a bit of clarity on my point</u>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12596,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","user":"Alpharius","date":". 06-27-2017, 06:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","va